{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363908-npcs-and-you-how-to-make-your-players-care-about-chars","id":363908,"title":"NPCs and You: How to make your players care about chars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-08T16:30:15-08:00","id":363908,"title":"NPCs and You: How to make your players care about chars","content":"Hey, i been running a Mage game for a while and im not very focused on the Politics of mage or anything like that. I been reading some scenarios of Asencion and i see how important are chars like Voormas. My question is to all St, how you make your players involve with the canon NPCs and the political struggles within the game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T16:48:25-08:00","id":363919,"title":"","content":"It's a question of... &quot;yeah, and?&quot;<br /> <br /> The big NPC has to have fingers in a pie the PC cares about.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:38:23-08:00","id":364793,"title":"","content":"With NPCs in general, I find it's useful to make players feel indebted to the NPC, however slightly. Save them from something, do them a favor; even if it's not in the NPC's personality, even just say the PCs &quot;owe him&quot; for it and leave it hanging and uncollected. That nudges many PCs into taking the NPC's side, and once they've taken a side, it's easy to hook them into all kind of other NPCs by proxy. Read up on psychology about how to manipulate people, and do it to your players unashamed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T11:15:13-08:00","id":365549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363908-npcs-and-you-how-to-make-your-players-care-about-chars?p=364793#post364793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With NPCs in general, I find it's useful to make players feel indebted to the NPC, however slightly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, but I'd add too that my take usually works the opposite way. That is, I find it useful to have the NPC owe a boon, no matter how small, to one or more player character. For example, when our <b>Vampire</b> chronicle put the PCs of the troupe meeting Sabbat luminary Sascha Vykos and the Priscus had the characters owe it something, I got that 'and so what?' response mentioned above. However, when they later met Noddist scholar Beckett, and he wound up owing <i>them</i> a boon, the players were far more interested!<br /> <br /> That said, I'd also expand on what <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller\">Traveller</a></b> implied that you don't need to keep a slavish devotion to the 'canon' of any character. If you need a published character to do something that isn't within the written version, go for it! If the troupe won't respect the character, give that NPC something that the troupe will respect. All of this is to say that every NPC you introduce in a chronicle should be your own, regardless of that character's origin.<br /> <br /> Finally, I might also suggest that you feel free to just drop an established character into a role that a 'canon' character holds. That is to say, when presented with a choice of having a complete unknown Grand Master of the Euthanatoi<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Ooops! I dunno how that last thought gots all kinda not finished, but you kinda see where I'm going there, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","user":"Phaolan","date":". 01-11-2015, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T11:47:05-08:00","id":365567,"title":"","content":"Making the players and by extension PCs <i>hate</i> a given NPC is easy - so easy it often happens by accident. Any <i>other</i> response is more tricky.<br /> <br /> If you want them to trust an NPC, it's probably best if it be an Ally, Contact, or someone else they've invested points in. And don't make them betray the PCs. Too many players have learned to distrust any and all NPCs for this reason. Don't make a habit of having the enemy take them hostage or kill them either - GMs do this a bit too often to get an emotional response and this is where rootless orphan PCs come from. Indeed, some players with experiences like this will <i>not</i> trust a GM not to have NPCs mistreated or prone to betrayal - all you can do then is say you won't do it and keep to your word.<br /> <br /> Besides that, lay it on thick. As the <b>Players Guide</b> for <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> Revised notes, even a murderhobo Lone Wolf player <i>might</i> sympathise with and help out a helpless little kid. But even then it's touch and go.<br /> <br /> For the example of Voormas, let's say you want the PCs to know he's powerful and scary. Get some NPCs they're prepared to listen to (like Allies and Contacts) who are generally right about such things to mention he's powerful and scary, a few sessions before he's due to make an appearance in the game itself. When he does turn up, don't give him a lot of dialogue or make him do anything particularly flashy - although if anyone looks at him with supernatural senses they should get the impression of something impressive and unnerving. And consider what part he plays in the PCs' story - is he there as something to fight, something to actively avoid fighting, something to approach cautiously for some vital piece of information? If he's just there to be powerful and scary, he's really just an interesting piece of scenery and not worth that much thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T12:04:35-08:00","id":366533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/363908-npcs-and-you-how-to-make-your-players-care-about-chars?p=365567#post365567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want them to trust an NPC, it's probably best if it be an Ally, Contact, or someone else they've invested points in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with this, but <i>only</i> insofar as MY troupe doesn't but much stock in the notion of points-equals-value. I mention this because, as always, different groups have different expectations and requirements. On the other hand...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If he's just there to be powerful and scary, he's really just an interesting piece of scenery... </div> </div> </div>I DO agree with this! Make there be a REASON for him, or drop that jerk and put in someone who the characters already fear or already respect or already know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}